{"post_stream": {"posts": [{"id": 213919, "name": "Sirius Canopus", "username": "sirius-canopus", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/s/f5a326/{size}.png", "created_at": "2023-04-10T17:11:51.219Z", "cooked": "<p>Ok, sorry for noob question, but I am confused.</p>\n<p>I want to copy files from Camera connected via usb port. I can find device via <code>lsusb </code></p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-auto\">lsusb | grep Fuji                                                                                                                           \nBus 004 Device 003: ID 04cb:02f0 Fuji Photo Film Co., Ltd USB PTP Camera\n</code></pre>\n<p>But it is not visible via <code>lsblk</code></p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-auto\">lsblk                                                                                                                                   \nNAME        MAJ:MIN RM   SIZE RO TYPE MOUNTPOINTS\nloop0         7:0    0     4K  1 loop /var/lib/snapd/snap/bare/5\nloop1         7:1    0    22M  1 loop /var/lib/snapd/snap/bashtop/504\nloop2         7:2    0 116.8M  1 loop /var/lib/snapd/snap/core/14784\nloop3         7:3    0 116.8M  1 loop /var/lib/snapd/snap/core/14946\nloop4         7:4    0  55.6M  1 loop /var/lib/snapd/snap/core18/2714\nloop5         7:5    0  55.6M  1 loop /var/lib/snapd/snap/core18/2721\nloop6         7:6    0  63.3M  1 loop /var/lib/snapd/snap/core20/1828\nloop7         7:7    0  63.3M  1 loop /var/lib/snapd/snap/core20/1852\nloop8         7:8    0    73M  1 loop /var/lib/snapd/snap/core22/583\nloop9         7:9    0    73M  1 loop /var/lib/snapd/snap/core22/607\nloop10        7:10   0 164.8M  1 loop /var/lib/snapd/snap/gnome-3-28-1804/161\nloop11        7:11   0   1.4M  1 loop /var/lib/snapd/snap/dust/11\nloop12        7:12   0 164.8M  1 loop /var/lib/snapd/snap/gnome-3-28-1804/194\nloop13        7:13   0   219M  1 loop /var/lib/snapd/snap/gnome-3-34-1804/77\nloop14        7:14   0 218.4M  1 loop /var/lib/snapd/snap/gnome-3-34-1804/90\nloop15        7:15   0 349.7M  1 loop /var/lib/snapd/snap/gnome-3-38-2004/137\nloop16        7:16   0  91.7M  1 loop /var/lib/snapd/snap/gtk-common-themes/1535\nloop17        7:17   0   145M  1 loop /var/lib/snapd/snap/notepadqq/855\nloop18        7:18   0 188.3M  1 loop /var/lib/snapd/snap/postman/184\nloop19        7:19   0  49.8M  1 loop /var/lib/snapd/snap/snapd/18357\nloop20        7:20   0  49.8M  1 loop /var/lib/snapd/snap/snapd/18596\nloop21        7:21   0 169.4M  1 loop /var/lib/snapd/snap/spotify/60\nloop22        7:22   0 156.6M  1 loop /var/lib/snapd/snap/spotify/63\nloop23        7:23   0 362.1M  1 loop /var/lib/snapd/snap/telegram-desktop/4578\nloop24        7:24   0 362.1M  1 loop /var/lib/snapd/snap/telegram-desktop/4654\nloop25        7:25   0 944.1M  1 loop /var/lib/snapd/snap/xonotic/64\nzram0       252:0    0     8G  0 disk [SWAP]\nnvme1n1     259:0    0   1.9T  0 disk \n├─nvme1n1p1 259:5    0   260M  0 part \n├─nvme1n1p2 259:6    0    16M  0 part \n├─nvme1n1p3 259:7    0   1.9T  0 part \n└─nvme1n1p4 259:8    0     2G  0 part \nnvme0n1     259:1    0 931.5G  0 disk \n├─nvme0n1p1 259:2    0   600M  0 part /boot/efi\n├─nvme0n1p2 259:3    0     1G  0 part /boot\n└─nvme0n1p3 259:4    0 929.9G  0 part /home\n\n</code></pre>\n<p>Also, can you please describe list of actions:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Mount</li>\n<li>Copy</li>\n<li>Unmount?</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Thank you in advance</p>", "post_number": 1, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 6, "updated_at": "2023-06-22T14:40:31.216Z", "reply_count": 2, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 357, "reads": 22, "readers_count": 21, "score": 1799.4, "yours": false, "topic_id": 80683, "topic_slug": "copy-from-usb-device", "display_username": "Sirius Canopus", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 2, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 7737, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/copy-from-usb-device/80683/1", "event": null, "calendar_details": [], "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 213921, "name": "Vladislav Grigoryev", "username": "vgaetera", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/vgaetera/{size}/2552_2.png", "created_at": "2023-04-10T18:01:01.368Z", "cooked": "<p>It looks like there is no corresponding block device.<br>\nBe sure to enable data storage access over USB on the camera itself.</p>", "post_number": 2, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 6, "updated_at": "2023-04-11T10:50:41.919Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": 1, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 0, "reads": 19, "readers_count": 18, "score": 3.8, "yours": false, "topic_id": 80683, "topic_slug": "copy-from-usb-device", "display_username": "Vladislav Grigoryev", "primary_group_name": "ask-fedora", "flair_name": "ask-fedora", "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": "", "flair_color": "", "flair_group_id": 53, "badges_granted": [], "version": 2, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "", "reply_to_user": {"id": 7737, "username": "sirius-canopus", "name": "Sirius Canopus", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/s/f5a326/{size}.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 549, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 3, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/copy-from-usb-device/80683/2", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 213952, "name": "George N. White III", "username": "gnwiii", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/gnwiii/{size}/34440_2.png", "created_at": "2023-04-10T21:03:04.091Z", "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"sirius-canopus\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"80683\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/s/f5a326/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Sirius Canopus:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p><code>Fuji Photo Film Co., Ltd USB PTP Camera</code></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Picture_Transfer_Protocol\">PTP in this context stands for Picture Transfer Protocol</a>, not to be confused with Precision Time Protocol.</p>\n<p>If the camera provides a mass storage option then you can work with images using standard file operations.  Some photo apps may have PTP support, but I don’t think PTP is widely used.</p>", "post_number": 3, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 6, "updated_at": "2023-04-10T21:03:04.091Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 1, "incoming_link_count": 7, "reads": 18, "readers_count": 17, "score": 73.6, "yours": false, "topic_id": 80683, "topic_slug": "copy-from-usb-device", "display_username": "George N. White III", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Picture_Transfer_Protocol", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "Picture Transfer Protocol - Wikipedia", "clicks": 0}], "read": true, "user_title": "", "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 2}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 4552, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 3, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/copy-from-usb-device/80683/3", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 2}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 2, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 213989, "name": "Villy Kruse", "username": "vekruse", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/v/aad0ee/{size}.png", "created_at": "2023-04-11T06:18:14.879Z", "cooked": "<p>For PTP devices you need the <code>gvfs-gphoto2</code> package.  In xfce environment, when you plug in the camara, it will show up on the desktop and you can then click on it to open it.</p>\n<p>I assume gnome has something similar.</p>", "post_number": 4, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 6, "updated_at": "2023-04-11T06:18:14.879Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": 3, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 0, "reads": 14, "readers_count": 13, "score": 7.8, "yours": false, "topic_id": 80683, "topic_slug": "copy-from-usb-device", "display_username": "Villy Kruse", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "reply_to_user": {"id": 4552, "username": "gnwiii", "name": "George N. White III", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/gnwiii/{size}/34440_2.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 8762, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 3, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/copy-from-usb-device/80683/4", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "eureka", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 1, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 213990, "name": "Villy Kruse", "username": "vekruse", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/v/aad0ee/{size}.png", "created_at": "2023-04-11T06:21:13.229Z", "cooked": "<p>Off topic,  you may want to remove some of the old unused snap packages.  Run<br>\n<code>snap list --all</code> to see the unused ones.</p>", "post_number": 5, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 6, "updated_at": "2023-04-11T06:21:13.229Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 2, "reads": 14, "readers_count": 13, "score": 27.8, "yours": false, "topic_id": 80683, "topic_slug": "copy-from-usb-device", "display_username": "Villy Kruse", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 1}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 8762, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 3, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/copy-from-usb-device/80683/5", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 1, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": null}, {"id": 214011, "name": "Sirius Canopus", "username": "sirius-canopus", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/s/f5a326/{size}.png", "created_at": "2023-04-11T10:33:37.868Z", "cooked": "<p>Ok, thank you. Basically now Nautilus (Files) but not other file managers can see the Camera USB.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-auto\">gphoto2 --auto-detect                                                                                                        \nModel                          Port                                            \n----------------------------------------------------------\nUSB PTP Class Camera           usb:004,004    \n</code></pre>\n<p>Bu still if I want to</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-auto\">gphoto2 --list-files                                                                                                            \n                                                                               \n*** Error ***              \nAn error occurred in the io-library ('Could not claim the USB device'): Could not claim interface 0 (Device or resource busy). Make sure no other program (gvfs-gphoto2-volume-monitor) or kernel module (such as sdc2xx, stv680, spca50x) is using the device and you have read/write access to the device.\n*** Error (-53: 'Could not claim the USB device') ***  \n</code></pre>\n<p>So i can access photos, but not via terminal yet</p>", "post_number": 6, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 6, "updated_at": "2